# The build context is ./dashboard, so the repository root .dockerignore does
# not apply here and this file is the only thing excluding anything.
#
# `node_modules` matters most. The Dockerfile runs `npm ci` and then `COPY . .`,
# so without this line a developer who has installed locally copies their host
# `node_modules` over the one the image just built -- Windows or macOS binaries
# landing in an Alpine image, and `npm run build` failing for reasons that have
# nothing to do with the commit. CI never hits it, because a fresh checkout has
# no `node_modules`: the CI build and a local build of the same Dockerfile were
# not the same build, which is the class of problem the image job added
# alongside this file exists to close.
node_modules

# Generated by the build inside the image; copying a stale host copy in first
# only invites confusion about which one was served.
dist
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# Never useful in the image, and `.env` in a build context is worth excluding
# on its own.
.env
.env.*
.git
.gitignore
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
